1
00:00:28,528 --> 00:00:29,946
TAKE CHARGE OF MY HEART

2
00:00:39,539 --> 00:00:40,373
Okay.

3
00:00:40,457 --> 00:00:41,708
I will

4
00:00:43,084 --> 00:00:44,919
save you, Mr. Baek Ho-rang.

5
00:00:52,927 --> 00:00:55,680
Then move into my place tomorrow.

6
00:00:55,764 --> 00:00:57,474
Tomorrow? That soon?

7
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:00,810
I need to tell my sister and brother.

8
00:01:00,894 --> 00:01:02,228
Give it a rest already.

9
00:01:02,312 --> 00:01:03,146
It's not fair.

10
00:01:03,813 --> 00:01:06,149
I wanted to eat that one.

11
00:01:06,232 --> 00:01:07,776
Just eat whatever.

12
00:01:07,859 --> 00:01:10,153
-Hide.
-Why should I hide?

13
00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:14,032
-I said just eat whatever!
-But I picked that one!

14
00:01:14,115 --> 00:01:15,492
Hey, Yong-gi!

15
00:01:15,575 --> 00:01:16,910
You're stressing me out.

16
00:01:16,993 --> 00:01:17,869
Huh?

17
00:01:18,620 --> 00:01:21,498
-What are you doing here?
-Our baby sister is here!

18
00:01:21,581 --> 00:01:23,124
For our baby sister…

19
00:01:24,167 --> 00:01:26,461
Here, have this.
It's the most expensive one.

20
00:01:26,544 --> 00:01:28,004
Sweet! It looks good.

21
00:01:29,923 --> 00:01:31,091
-Have you eaten?
-Yeah.

22
00:01:31,174 --> 00:01:32,425
What about you guys?

23
00:01:32,926 --> 00:01:34,344
She wanted ice cream first.

24
00:01:34,427 --> 00:01:35,386
You haven't eaten?

25
00:01:35,470 --> 00:01:37,430
-We ate earlier.
-You call that dinner?

26
00:01:37,514 --> 00:01:39,474
You scarfed it down. What's your problem?

27
00:01:39,557 --> 00:01:41,309
-Come on, guys.
-Jeez.

28
00:01:58,827 --> 00:02:00,286
I'm here to pick you up.

29
00:02:07,585 --> 00:02:08,878
Is anything bothering you?

30
00:02:09,546 --> 00:02:10,463
Well…

31
00:02:11,005 --> 00:02:12,173
No, I just…

32
00:02:12,257 --> 00:02:14,884
I can't believe this is really happening.

33
00:02:16,261 --> 00:02:19,430
And I feel bad
for lying to my sister and brother.

34
00:02:20,557 --> 00:02:24,018
The company's giving you a studio?
Just like that?

35
00:02:24,102 --> 00:02:24,936
Yeah.

36
00:02:25,019 --> 00:02:27,856
I knew our Bo-bae
would make it big someday.

37
00:02:28,815 --> 00:02:30,984
In three months,
Na Ji-hye will be married,

38
00:02:31,067 --> 00:02:33,153
I'll be in Daejeon,
and this home will be gone.

39
00:02:33,236 --> 00:02:35,572
Bo-bae, it all worked out, huh?

40
00:02:37,157 --> 00:02:39,367
You're not making this up, are you?

41
00:02:39,450 --> 00:02:42,412
Come on. Why would I make that up?

42
00:02:43,621 --> 00:02:45,039
I guess that's true.

43
00:02:46,708 --> 00:02:49,460
Thank you
for making this difficult decision.

44
00:02:49,544 --> 00:02:52,005
If it weren't for you, Mr. Baek

45
00:02:52,839 --> 00:02:54,424
would've been in grave danger.

46
00:02:55,383 --> 00:02:56,509
Right.

47
00:02:56,593 --> 00:02:59,387
As for your role, Ms. Na Bo-bae,

48
00:03:00,305 --> 00:03:03,183
it is strictly limited to charging.

49
00:03:03,892 --> 00:03:04,976
Please keep that in mind.

50
00:03:05,977 --> 00:03:07,020
I will.

51
00:03:07,520 --> 00:03:11,399
Well… Mr. Yoon?

52
00:03:11,983 --> 00:03:12,817
Yes?

53
00:03:13,776 --> 00:03:17,947
Well, it sounds like Mr. Baek Ho-rang
holds a very high position.

54
00:03:18,615 --> 00:03:20,783
What exactly does he do?

55
00:03:20,867 --> 00:03:23,703
He's the senior managing director
of TS Resort.

56
00:03:23,786 --> 00:03:24,621
TS?

57
00:03:25,330 --> 00:03:26,706
That's a huge company.

58
00:03:27,665 --> 00:03:28,917
Senior managing director?

59
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:31,461
Doesn't that basically make him a chaebol?

60
00:03:32,378 --> 00:03:35,590
More precisely,
he's a third-generation chaebol.

61
00:04:01,491 --> 00:04:03,451
This is Mr. Baek Ho-rang's house?

62
00:04:03,534 --> 00:04:04,369
Yes.

63
00:04:06,746 --> 00:04:09,666
You'll be staying here
for the next three months.

64
00:04:21,552 --> 00:04:22,512
We meet again.

65
00:04:24,138 --> 00:04:25,348
We do indeed.

66
00:04:26,266 --> 00:04:28,142
You shoved me into a corner yesterday.

67
00:04:29,269 --> 00:04:31,104
I thought you didn't want to see me.

68
00:04:31,187 --> 00:04:32,355
Well, it's just that…

69
00:04:32,855 --> 00:04:35,108
I didn't really know how to explain it.

70
00:04:35,191 --> 00:04:36,901
And you seem just fine.

71
00:04:40,446 --> 00:04:42,323
So petty.

72
00:05:18,985 --> 00:05:21,195
Your house is super nice.

73
00:05:21,904 --> 00:05:24,115
Can I take some pictures? For research.

74
00:05:24,198 --> 00:05:25,074
No, you can't.

75
00:05:25,158 --> 00:05:29,037
I won't show anyone.
I'll never see a house like this again.

76
00:05:29,120 --> 00:05:31,497
If any photos get leaked, I'll sue you.

77
00:05:31,581 --> 00:05:32,915
So go ahead and take them.

78
00:05:34,250 --> 00:05:35,126
That's spot on.

79
00:05:35,209 --> 00:05:36,210
What is?

80
00:05:36,294 --> 00:05:37,837
You always see them in dramas.

81
00:05:37,920 --> 00:05:40,757
The man who shut himself off,
scarred by a painful past,

82
00:05:40,840 --> 00:05:42,842
only to be changed by true love:

83
00:05:42,925 --> 00:05:45,428
the rude-ass third-gen chaebol heir.

84
00:05:45,511 --> 00:05:49,098
Sorry, but this is reality, not a drama.

85
00:05:49,182 --> 00:05:50,641
And "rude-ass"? What do you--

86
00:06:02,528 --> 00:06:04,530
Stop looking around and come here.

87
00:06:22,131 --> 00:06:25,134
This is as far as you're allowed.

88
00:06:25,218 --> 00:06:29,931
In other words,
don't wander off anywhere else without…

89
00:06:37,271 --> 00:06:39,190
Looks like you eat pretty well.

90
00:06:39,273 --> 00:06:41,150
My housekeeper keeps it stocked for me.

91
00:06:41,234 --> 00:06:45,071
So chaebol have housekeepers, huh?

92
00:06:45,154 --> 00:06:47,365
How did you explain who I am to--

93
00:06:52,787 --> 00:06:53,704
Do I really

94
00:06:54,288 --> 00:06:55,123
have to explain?

95
00:06:56,124 --> 00:06:58,126
Well, I mean,

96
00:06:58,209 --> 00:07:00,294
we'll be running into each other a lot.

97
00:07:00,378 --> 00:07:02,505
That won't be necessary. Don't worry.

98
00:07:02,588 --> 00:07:03,840
Our arrangement

99
00:07:03,923 --> 00:07:07,051
stays strictly between us.

100
00:07:10,847 --> 00:07:12,807
Why did you put that on?

101
00:07:12,890 --> 00:07:13,850
Take it off.

102
00:07:36,581 --> 00:07:38,040
This is my room.

103
00:07:39,333 --> 00:07:42,170
It's bigger than my living room.

104
00:07:44,005 --> 00:07:47,049
Wow, this bed is massive.

105
00:07:52,597 --> 00:07:53,639
Feel free to lie down.

106
00:07:54,682 --> 00:07:55,516
What?

107
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:59,145
If we're going to have physical contact,
we'll have to share a bed at times.

108
00:08:02,315 --> 00:08:04,650
Why would we have physical contact in bed?

109
00:08:04,734 --> 00:08:07,695
Would you rather do it in public?

110
00:08:29,258 --> 00:08:30,551
Actually…

111
00:08:32,595 --> 00:08:33,596
I need…

112
00:08:37,767 --> 00:08:39,185
a recharge now.

113
00:08:53,199 --> 00:08:54,700
What are you doing?

114
00:08:59,872 --> 00:09:00,998
My room.

115
00:09:01,541 --> 00:09:02,833
I want to see my room.

116
00:09:12,802 --> 00:09:13,844
Wait.

117
00:09:13,928 --> 00:09:16,347
I want to see my room.
Why are we back outside?

118
00:09:18,975 --> 00:09:19,809
Huh?

119
00:09:30,444 --> 00:09:34,073
This is where you'll be staying
from now on.

120
00:09:35,283 --> 00:09:36,117
What?

121
00:09:43,124 --> 00:09:44,250
But this is

122
00:09:44,875 --> 00:09:46,210
a storage room.

123
00:09:47,628 --> 00:09:49,213
This is your room.

124
00:09:52,883 --> 00:09:54,719
Why put me here when you have that nice…

125
00:09:54,802 --> 00:09:57,805
Charging my heart
is the whole point of our contract.

126
00:09:57,888 --> 00:10:01,267
It's exactly ten meters
from here to my room.

127
00:10:01,350 --> 00:10:04,395
So charging shouldn't be a problem.

128
00:10:04,478 --> 00:10:06,314
There's no need for us to live together.

129
00:10:06,397 --> 00:10:07,732
-But--
-Come on.

130
00:10:07,815 --> 00:10:09,191
Let's go over our contract.

131
00:10:37,136 --> 00:10:38,054
Well…

132
00:10:38,137 --> 00:10:41,849
-If you want, I can redecorate--
-I do.

133
00:10:48,105 --> 00:10:48,981
Have a seat.

134
00:11:00,701 --> 00:11:02,161
Look it over.

135
00:11:05,539 --> 00:11:07,667
SENIOR MANAGING DIRECTOR
BAEK HO-RANG

136
00:11:09,585 --> 00:11:10,419
What?

137
00:11:12,380 --> 00:11:14,256
This whole thing is the contract?

138
00:11:14,340 --> 00:11:15,883
My life is at stake here.

139
00:11:15,966 --> 00:11:18,928
-This is the bare minimum.
-How am I supposed to read all this?

140
00:11:19,011 --> 00:11:21,138
I've only listed my terms so far.

141
00:11:21,222 --> 00:11:23,724
You can add yours now.

142
00:11:27,395 --> 00:11:30,022
"Na Bo-bae shall charge
Baek Ho-rang's artificial heart

143
00:11:30,106 --> 00:11:32,108
every morning at 7:30…

144
00:11:35,361 --> 00:11:37,613
by holding his hand."

145
00:11:37,697 --> 00:11:41,659
I'm never up before 10:00,
especially after writing all night.

146
00:11:41,742 --> 00:11:44,245
I work in an office. I start at 8:30.

147
00:11:44,328 --> 00:11:47,915
This is the only way I can fully charge
and stick to my morning routine.

148
00:11:51,711 --> 00:11:53,295
"Under normal circumstances,

149
00:11:53,379 --> 00:11:57,591
Baek Ho-rang shall not request any method
of recharging other than hand-holding."

150
00:11:57,675 --> 00:12:01,345
"However, if the battery level
falls below 10%,

151
00:12:01,429 --> 00:12:05,725
Na Bo-bae shall, without exception,
through close physical contact…"

152
00:12:06,892 --> 00:12:07,977
"Close"?

153
00:12:10,938 --> 00:12:12,982
What constitutes "close physical contact"?

154
00:12:13,065 --> 00:12:16,902
Contact between mucosal surfaces.

155
00:12:18,946 --> 00:12:19,780
What?

156
00:12:19,864 --> 00:12:20,698
Well…

157
00:12:22,116 --> 00:12:24,368
Like kissing or…

158
00:12:25,244 --> 00:12:26,412
something beyond that.

159
00:12:28,581 --> 00:12:31,250
In any case,
it only applies in emergencies

160
00:12:31,333 --> 00:12:33,002
when the battery drops below 10%.

161
00:12:33,085 --> 00:12:33,919
Oh.

162
00:12:35,838 --> 00:12:37,631
I mean, we'll be living together.

163
00:12:37,715 --> 00:12:41,844
It's not like the battery
will ever drop below 10%, right?

164
00:12:41,927 --> 00:12:43,179
I agree.

165
00:12:43,262 --> 00:12:45,389
It's just a formality. Don't worry.

166
00:12:45,890 --> 00:12:47,558
And I have no desire

167
00:12:47,641 --> 00:12:49,685
to have "close" physical contact

168
00:12:49,769 --> 00:12:51,353
with you, Ms. Na Bo-bae.

169
00:12:51,437 --> 00:12:52,438
That's great.

170
00:12:52,521 --> 00:12:55,191
If it weren't for my script,

171
00:12:55,274 --> 00:12:57,610
I wouldn't even share a table with you.

172
00:12:58,110 --> 00:12:59,361
If you say so.

173
00:13:05,284 --> 00:13:06,869
Where do I add my terms?

174
00:13:19,590 --> 00:13:21,550
DO ONE ROMANCE BUCKET LIST ITEM EACH WEEK

175
00:13:21,634 --> 00:13:23,427
"Romance bucket list"?

176
00:13:23,511 --> 00:13:27,515
There are a few dates
I want to write into my script.

177
00:13:28,224 --> 00:13:33,145
I'm just a teensy bit weaker
on the romance front,

178
00:13:33,771 --> 00:13:36,565
so I wanted to experience it
before I write it.

179
00:13:37,066 --> 00:13:40,194
It's nice and clear.
Share the list with me later.

180
00:13:40,277 --> 00:13:41,195
Sure.

181
00:13:42,238 --> 00:13:44,281
The next one is right below it.

182
00:13:46,075 --> 00:13:48,619
"During this agreement,
neither Na Bo-bae nor Baek Ho-rang

183
00:13:48,702 --> 00:13:50,955
shall see anyone of the opposite gender,

184
00:13:51,038 --> 00:13:54,083
and shall be sincere with one another."

185
00:13:55,292 --> 00:13:57,294
I wasn't planning on seeing anyone anyway.

186
00:13:57,878 --> 00:14:01,549
You sure you don't have a boyfriend?

187
00:14:01,632 --> 00:14:03,342
I told you, I don't.

188
00:14:03,425 --> 00:14:05,302
You're all I have.

189
00:14:09,974 --> 00:14:11,100
What I'm saying is…

190
00:14:12,184 --> 00:14:16,021
I didn't mean you're all I have
in that way.

191
00:14:16,605 --> 00:14:17,731
As a man.

192
00:14:18,315 --> 00:14:20,401
You're the only man I've got?

193
00:14:20,484 --> 00:14:22,361
Okay, I get what you mean.

194
00:14:22,444 --> 00:14:23,445
Yeah.

195
00:14:24,613 --> 00:14:25,531
I get it.

196
00:14:31,704 --> 00:14:33,789
-We're all set now, right?
-Yes.

197
00:14:35,332 --> 00:14:36,542
One more thing.

198
00:14:37,126 --> 00:14:39,420
I'll be the one to initiate charging.

199
00:14:39,503 --> 00:14:41,422
Whether it's holding hands, hugging,

200
00:14:42,631 --> 00:14:44,633
or close physical contact.

201
00:14:44,717 --> 00:14:48,220
Since my body is the charger,
I'll decide when and how it happens.

202
00:14:48,304 --> 00:14:49,263
All right.

203
00:14:50,431 --> 00:14:52,308
I'll revise it accordingly.

204
00:14:57,354 --> 00:14:58,230
Oh, right.

205
00:14:59,481 --> 00:15:00,900
After we sign,

206
00:15:01,901 --> 00:15:03,819
we'll test the charging rate.

207
00:15:04,820 --> 00:15:05,654
Is that okay?

208
00:15:06,447 --> 00:15:08,115
Yes, that's fine.

209
00:15:08,198 --> 00:15:12,453
We'll have to hold hands, hug,

210
00:15:12,536 --> 00:15:13,913
and maybe…

211
00:15:15,915 --> 00:15:17,166
even do more.

212
00:15:19,251 --> 00:15:21,462
I mean, it's just a test.

213
00:15:21,962 --> 00:15:23,005
It's fine.

214
00:15:24,340 --> 00:15:25,257
All right.

215
00:15:25,925 --> 00:15:28,385
I'll take that as a yes.

216
00:15:54,787 --> 00:15:56,664
MY SIS

217
00:15:58,916 --> 00:15:59,750
Hey, Ji-hye.

218
00:15:59,833 --> 00:16:02,086
Hey, are you at the studio?

219
00:16:02,169 --> 00:16:03,504
How is it? Is it okay?

220
00:16:03,587 --> 00:16:05,589
Oh, this place?

221
00:16:06,131 --> 00:16:08,384
It's really nice.

222
00:16:08,467 --> 00:16:12,346
It's spacious,
and it's got all the latest equipment.

223
00:16:14,515 --> 00:16:16,433
And it's got an amazing view.

224
00:16:16,934 --> 00:16:19,478
Since the TV station
arranged the studio for you,

225
00:16:19,561 --> 00:16:21,188
we probably shouldn't go, right?

226
00:16:21,689 --> 00:16:22,815
You okay living alone?

227
00:16:22,898 --> 00:16:25,859
Of course I am.

228
00:16:26,360 --> 00:16:29,989
I see this as my last chance.

229
00:16:30,614 --> 00:16:32,741
I really want to make it.

230
00:16:32,825 --> 00:16:35,160
I want to see my name on a drama,

231
00:16:35,244 --> 00:16:38,706
and I want to proudly call myself
a drama writer.

232
00:16:39,373 --> 00:16:45,212
I don't want to feel small
and ashamed of my scripts anymore.

233
00:16:45,295 --> 00:16:49,341
Tell me if anyone looks down on you.
They won't get away with it.

234
00:16:49,425 --> 00:16:52,261
Don't worry about anything else.
Just focus on writing, okay?

235
00:16:52,344 --> 00:16:55,139
Now all you have to do
is become a star writer, Na Bo-bae.

236
00:16:56,390 --> 00:16:57,474
All right.

237
00:16:57,558 --> 00:16:58,684
Is it Bo-bae?

238
00:16:58,767 --> 00:17:00,185
Go away.

239
00:17:00,269 --> 00:17:02,229
Bo-bae! Our Bo-bae is the best!

240
00:17:02,312 --> 00:17:03,897
-Stop!
-You're Korea's best writer!

241
00:17:04,732 --> 00:17:05,733
I said go away. Go.

242
00:17:05,816 --> 00:17:09,528
Ji-hye, I have to go.
I need to work on my script.

243
00:17:09,611 --> 00:17:11,196
Okay. Hey, Bo-bae.

244
00:17:11,280 --> 00:17:12,239
Yeah?

245
00:17:12,906 --> 00:17:14,908
Give it your best shot.

246
00:17:15,409 --> 00:17:17,494
But if things get tough,
you can always come back.

247
00:17:17,578 --> 00:17:18,579
You know that, right?

248
00:17:20,622 --> 00:17:22,291
Yeah, of course.

249
00:17:23,625 --> 00:17:24,585
Okay.

250
00:17:35,054 --> 00:17:35,971
That's right.

251
00:17:37,890 --> 00:17:40,267
I should at least give it my best shot.

252
00:18:10,422 --> 00:18:12,674
ROMANCE DRAMA WRITING TECHNIQUES

253
00:19:18,657 --> 00:19:22,452
Charging starts at 7:30 every morning.
It's already 7:40.

254
00:19:22,536 --> 00:19:24,371
I'm sorry.

255
00:19:25,164 --> 00:19:27,416
Morning charging
is just holding hands, right?

256
00:19:27,499 --> 00:19:30,586
Be on time from now on.
I can't stand people breaking the rules.

257
00:19:30,669 --> 00:19:33,213
It's clearly stated in the contract.

258
00:19:33,297 --> 00:19:34,673
Fine.

259
00:19:34,756 --> 00:19:36,049
Here.

260
00:20:00,532 --> 00:20:03,994
I'll come straight home after work.
We'll test the charging rate tonight.

261
00:20:06,288 --> 00:20:07,289
Are you crazy?

262
00:20:07,915 --> 00:20:09,791
I told you to wait six months!

263
00:20:09,875 --> 00:20:13,128
We just signed a contract last month.
Why'd you go and sign another?

264
00:20:13,712 --> 00:20:16,548
Are you trying to get caught?

265
00:20:16,632 --> 00:20:18,634
-My head's killing me.
-My apologies.

266
00:20:24,181 --> 00:20:25,849
I guess our VP was in a hurry.

267
00:20:25,933 --> 00:20:27,017
TS HOTEL FOOD SUPPLY CONTRACT

268
00:20:27,100 --> 00:20:28,352
A mistake like this? Really?

269
00:20:28,435 --> 00:20:30,437
Yoon Dong-seok!

270
00:20:30,520 --> 00:20:33,649
Do you have any idea
how important this is?

271
00:20:33,732 --> 00:20:35,776
Imagine if my husband finds out.

272
00:20:35,859 --> 00:20:38,278
You won't be leaving in one piece!

273
00:20:38,362 --> 00:20:40,155
My deepest apologies, ma'am.

274
00:20:40,239 --> 00:20:42,491
Hey, Baek.
You'll get wrinkles from frowning.

275
00:20:42,574 --> 00:20:45,077
"Hey, Baek"? Is that any way
to address your mother?

276
00:20:45,661 --> 00:20:47,496
You think this doesn't concern you?

277
00:20:47,579 --> 00:20:50,707
Baek Ho-rang's successor announcement
is on hold.

278
00:20:50,791 --> 00:20:53,335
This is our chance to get ahead.

279
00:20:53,418 --> 00:20:55,671
If they find out we messed with the money,

280
00:20:55,754 --> 00:20:57,172
we're toast.

281
00:20:57,673 --> 00:20:59,174
As you can see,

282
00:20:59,258 --> 00:21:03,845
Mr. Ji Eun-ho landed his first lead role
with Ms. Na's debut work, Wistful Youth.

283
00:21:07,015 --> 00:21:08,976
Well, you're a fan.

284
00:21:09,059 --> 00:21:11,520
That's why you're so nice about my work.

285
00:21:12,020 --> 00:21:13,814
That damn romance.

286
00:21:14,690 --> 00:21:17,025
So that was Ji Eun-ho.

287
00:21:17,109 --> 00:21:19,236
He only backed out of the meeting

288
00:21:19,319 --> 00:21:21,446
because Ms. Na was hospitalized.

289
00:21:22,406 --> 00:21:24,366
If we can get Ms. Na on our side first…

290
00:21:24,449 --> 00:21:25,450
Hold on, sir.

291
00:21:25,534 --> 00:21:27,327
-Please don't.
-His schedule is full.

292
00:21:27,411 --> 00:21:29,413
If you can schedule a meeting later…

293
00:21:29,496 --> 00:21:30,789
Wait, sir! You can't…

294
00:21:33,750 --> 00:21:34,584
Hey.

295
00:21:35,669 --> 00:21:36,920
You think you own this place?

296
00:21:43,176 --> 00:21:45,971
Sir, Mr. Baek has an appointment shortly.

297
00:21:46,680 --> 00:21:47,931
If you could set up--

298
00:21:48,015 --> 00:21:50,058
I was passing by and thought I'd drop in.

299
00:21:50,726 --> 00:21:53,270
Thought I'd come see my dear cousin.

300
00:21:55,731 --> 00:21:57,232
It's your birthday soon.

301
00:21:57,816 --> 00:21:59,234
Want anything?

302
00:21:59,901 --> 00:22:02,612
Since when do you care about my birthday?

303
00:22:03,196 --> 00:22:04,573
Get out. I'm busy.

304
00:22:04,656 --> 00:22:07,242
Come on. Everyone here is busy.

305
00:22:07,326 --> 00:22:10,912
You always act like
you're so important and busy.

306
00:22:10,996 --> 00:22:12,998
Hey, Kim.

307
00:22:13,081 --> 00:22:15,000
Get me an iced Americano. Extra shot.

308
00:22:15,083 --> 00:22:16,251
He's Mr. Yoon.

309
00:22:17,085 --> 00:22:17,919
Don't bring it.

310
00:22:20,922 --> 00:22:24,509
If you want coffee, go to a café.
If you want to have fun, go to a club.

311
00:22:26,345 --> 00:22:29,931
No one's got time for you here.

312
00:22:42,903 --> 00:22:43,737
Mom.

313
00:22:48,867 --> 00:22:50,118
I'm certain.

314
00:22:52,746 --> 00:22:54,373
He doesn't know yet.

315
00:23:07,469 --> 00:23:09,805
Your name came up
during the table read with Director Yeom.

316
00:23:09,888 --> 00:23:13,725
-Is she messing with me?
-So I thought I'd text. Good luck!

317
00:23:21,233 --> 00:23:25,821
Thanks, Ju-hee… Hope your drama blows up…

318
00:23:30,534 --> 00:23:33,453
I'm the one who needs to blow up.

319
00:23:36,832 --> 00:23:40,210
This is seriously driving me nuts.

320
00:23:55,350 --> 00:23:56,226
No.

321
00:23:57,686 --> 00:23:59,396
I don't have time for this.

322
00:24:14,202 --> 00:24:16,830
I've been waiting for you,
Mr. Baek Ho-rang.

323
00:24:22,127 --> 00:24:24,546
"Romance Bucket List."

324
00:24:25,505 --> 00:24:28,049
"Drink together until late at night."

325
00:24:28,133 --> 00:24:30,719
"Late-night walk by the Hangang River."

326
00:24:30,802 --> 00:24:32,971
"Nighttime theme park date."

327
00:24:33,763 --> 00:24:36,141
Did I overdo the whole nighttime thing?

328
00:24:36,224 --> 00:24:38,268
-Do we have to do them in order?
-No.

329
00:24:38,351 --> 00:24:39,686
That doesn't matter.

330
00:24:39,769 --> 00:24:40,729
DO A CHAEBOL FLEX

331
00:24:40,812 --> 00:24:42,314
"Chaebol flex"?

332
00:24:43,482 --> 00:24:44,316
What's this?

333
00:24:46,902 --> 00:24:50,739
My female lead's a third-gen chaebol
facing an assassination threat.

334
00:24:50,822 --> 00:24:52,908
The male lead
is assigned as her bodyguard.

335
00:24:52,991 --> 00:24:54,868
As they slowly fall in love--

336
00:24:54,951 --> 00:24:56,077
Just the bottom line.

337
00:24:57,996 --> 00:25:00,874
I heard you were a chaebol.
Let's see you splash the cash.

338
00:25:02,250 --> 00:25:04,544
Isn't that kind of cliché and childish?

339
00:25:05,170 --> 00:25:07,130
Why is every drama about chaebols

340
00:25:07,214 --> 00:25:10,217
when there aren't even
a hundred conglomerates in Korea?

341
00:25:10,842 --> 00:25:12,469
Go ahead. Laugh all you want.

342
00:25:13,136 --> 00:25:15,931
I know the chaebol fantasies
in romance dramas

343
00:25:16,014 --> 00:25:17,933
are far-fetched and childish.

344
00:25:18,016 --> 00:25:19,309
Still,

345
00:25:20,936 --> 00:25:22,020
they're fun.

346
00:25:22,103 --> 00:25:23,772
Enough to keep people coming back.

347
00:25:26,358 --> 00:25:28,985
It doesn't matter
if it's cliché and childish.

348
00:25:29,069 --> 00:25:33,240
When you're watching something fun,
you forget everything else.

349
00:25:34,366 --> 00:25:38,036
The hardships, the loneliness, the pain.

350
00:25:38,995 --> 00:25:45,085
When you're watching something really fun,
it whisks you away to another world.

351
00:25:45,585 --> 00:25:48,255
Do you know how incredible that is?

352
00:25:49,339 --> 00:25:54,302
Look, I'll do everything you need.
The tests, the actual charging, all of it.

353
00:25:54,886 --> 00:25:58,640
In return, I want your full cooperation
with my romance.

354
00:26:00,016 --> 00:26:02,477
Of course. We have a contract.

355
00:26:02,561 --> 00:26:06,356
Let's start the charging rate test.
And then we'll cross one thing off

356
00:26:07,399 --> 00:26:08,316
your bucket list.

357
00:26:10,777 --> 00:26:12,028
RUBBER GLOVE

358
00:26:15,574 --> 00:26:18,368
Isn't it done yet?
It's been about ten minutes.

359
00:26:22,455 --> 00:26:25,083
HO-RANG'S ROOM
STORAGE ROOM

360
00:26:30,839 --> 00:26:31,840
PORTABLE CHARGER

361
00:26:31,923 --> 00:26:34,801
So it does charge 1% every ten minutes.

362
00:26:34,884 --> 00:26:35,885
All right. Next.

363
00:26:35,969 --> 00:26:37,095
CHARGING RATE TEST

364
00:26:40,807 --> 00:26:42,767
So? How much did it drop?

365
00:26:44,603 --> 00:26:46,229
When you're in the garage,

366
00:26:46,313 --> 00:26:49,149
charging only works as far as my room.

367
00:26:49,232 --> 00:26:51,359
BACKYARD
GARAGE

368
00:26:51,443 --> 00:26:55,155
And it seems to drop 1% every 15 minutes.

369
00:26:59,743 --> 00:27:00,702
If we're close,

370
00:27:00,785 --> 00:27:04,748
charging seems to take
only seven or eight minutes.

371
00:27:05,540 --> 00:27:08,501
It's not very consistent, is it?

372
00:27:09,169 --> 00:27:11,880
It seems to vary
with my condition and heart rate.

373
00:27:11,963 --> 00:27:15,133
We'd have to test
different levels of physical contact…

374
00:27:20,722 --> 00:27:22,974
to know for sure.

375
00:27:23,058 --> 00:27:23,892
Oh.

376
00:27:24,601 --> 00:27:28,438
Different levels of physical contact.
Right. We should test that.

377
00:27:28,938 --> 00:27:30,023
Holding hands?

378
00:27:43,787 --> 00:27:44,829
All right.

379
00:27:44,913 --> 00:27:47,624
Holding hands brings it up by 5%.

380
00:27:50,460 --> 00:27:51,586
Next would be…

381
00:27:53,588 --> 00:27:54,422
Let's try hugging.

382
00:27:54,506 --> 00:27:55,757
Yeah. Sure.

383
00:28:06,601 --> 00:28:08,019
Did I jump in too fast?

384
00:28:21,241 --> 00:28:23,201
Why is it beeping?

385
00:28:24,244 --> 00:28:25,453
A heart rate of 100?

386
00:28:25,537 --> 00:28:26,538
It's nothing!

387
00:28:27,080 --> 00:28:28,540
I mean, this…

388
00:28:31,126 --> 00:28:34,462
It probably charged up too fast.

389
00:28:38,341 --> 00:28:40,510
Hugging increases it by 10%.

390
00:28:48,351 --> 00:28:49,185
Well,

391
00:28:50,353 --> 00:28:51,521
I guess

392
00:28:52,355 --> 00:28:53,940
next would be

393
00:28:54,816 --> 00:28:56,067
kissing, right?

394
00:29:12,751 --> 00:29:14,753
As for kissing,

395
00:29:15,253 --> 00:29:16,838
I don't think we need to do that now.

396
00:29:16,921 --> 00:29:18,548
-Right? Yeah.
-Yes.

397
00:29:18,631 --> 00:29:20,425
I wasn't that curious anyway.

398
00:29:20,508 --> 00:29:22,385
I did kind of prepare myself for it.

399
00:29:22,469 --> 00:29:25,180
But if we don't, we don't.

400
00:29:26,598 --> 00:29:29,017
-Sounds like you want to.
-No way.

401
00:29:29,100 --> 00:29:30,685
Why would I? Not at all.

402
00:29:35,982 --> 00:29:37,358
You should get that.

403
00:29:41,070 --> 00:29:42,030
Yes, Mr. Yoon.

404
00:29:43,406 --> 00:29:44,240
Yes.

405
00:29:46,242 --> 00:29:47,076
Yeah.

406
00:29:50,663 --> 00:29:51,748
Yeah.

407
00:29:52,665 --> 00:29:53,541
Yeah, go ahead.

408
00:29:54,709 --> 00:29:57,170
Okay. I'll check. All right.

409
00:29:59,380 --> 00:30:01,674
Why are you grabbing my hand like that?

410
00:30:03,051 --> 00:30:03,885
Oh.

411
00:30:04,636 --> 00:30:05,637
I'm sorry.

412
00:30:08,139 --> 00:30:11,309
I thought we were doing
your bucket list today.

413
00:30:12,227 --> 00:30:13,186
Oh.

414
00:30:23,655 --> 00:30:25,365
SENIOR MANAGING DIRECTOR BAEK HO-RANG

415
00:30:41,172 --> 00:30:42,048
Yes.

416
00:30:43,383 --> 00:30:46,553
I just got off the phone with Mr. Baek.

417
00:30:58,690 --> 00:31:01,609
The night air feels so nice.

418
00:31:02,986 --> 00:31:04,237
It's humid.

419
00:31:08,449 --> 00:31:09,492
Damn it.

420
00:31:09,576 --> 00:31:12,787
If this were a drama, now would be
the perfect time to hold his hand.

421
00:31:13,830 --> 00:31:16,040
Should I say it's for the script
and do it?

422
00:31:30,513 --> 00:31:32,515
Is this really on your bucket list?

423
00:31:32,599 --> 00:31:33,433
Sorry?

424
00:31:34,058 --> 00:31:37,020
We're just walking.
Even in a drama, this would be boring.

425
00:31:38,980 --> 00:31:39,814
Well…

426
00:31:41,357 --> 00:31:43,568
Night walks have a certain romance,
you know.

427
00:31:44,402 --> 00:31:46,905
Like, there's this tingly tension

428
00:31:46,988 --> 00:31:50,325
when you're almost touching,
but not quite--

429
00:32:19,020 --> 00:32:20,355
That was close.

430
00:32:21,898 --> 00:32:23,650
I'm fine.

431
00:32:24,192 --> 00:32:25,276
I'm not.

432
00:32:25,360 --> 00:32:27,779
I don't think I got hit,

433
00:32:27,862 --> 00:32:29,447
but my heart rate's way up.

434
00:32:30,073 --> 00:32:32,325
That can't be good for my heart.

435
00:32:32,408 --> 00:32:34,285
It's dark out and he didn't even ring--

436
00:32:34,369 --> 00:32:36,329
What's the damn bell for, decoration?

437
00:32:36,412 --> 00:32:39,290
What if Mr. Baek got hurt in an accident
this late at night?

438
00:32:39,374 --> 00:32:41,501
Does he think he owns the Hangang River?

439
00:32:44,754 --> 00:32:45,588
Why are you…

440
00:32:45,672 --> 00:32:48,591
Enough walking.
Let's grab a bite and head home.

441
00:32:57,558 --> 00:32:59,185
Does he only care about himself?

442
00:32:59,268 --> 00:33:01,020
Romance, my ass.

443
00:33:01,521 --> 00:33:03,648
A romance? With a guy like him?

444
00:33:13,408 --> 00:33:15,201
All right. Here's your food.

445
00:33:15,284 --> 00:33:16,953
Thank you.

446
00:33:17,036 --> 00:33:18,079
Enjoy.

447
00:33:18,162 --> 00:33:19,497
Thank you.

448
00:33:20,289 --> 00:33:22,000
Looks yummy.

449
00:33:24,419 --> 00:33:26,462
There's so much.
You sure you don't want any?

450
00:33:29,257 --> 00:33:30,466
No, I'm good.

451
00:33:30,967 --> 00:33:34,178
You've never had chicken feet before?

452
00:33:34,262 --> 00:33:36,389
How can I eat something
that looks like this?

453
00:33:36,472 --> 00:33:38,975
It might not look appetizing,
but it's really good.

454
00:33:39,058 --> 00:33:41,144
-Like pig trotters.
-I don't eat those either.

455
00:33:43,312 --> 00:33:47,233
They've been serving chicken feet
for three generations.

456
00:33:47,316 --> 00:33:49,527
This is seriously good.

457
00:33:50,236 --> 00:33:52,071
It's good for your health too.

458
00:33:52,155 --> 00:33:53,614
It's practically medicine.

459
00:33:53,698 --> 00:33:56,743
How can something this spicy and salty
be medicine?

460
00:33:56,826 --> 00:33:59,037
-You're just fooling yourself.
-Yeah, I am.

461
00:33:59,120 --> 00:34:00,705
So what? It still tastes good.

462
00:34:06,127 --> 00:34:07,754
Seriously, it's so good.

463
00:34:08,463 --> 00:34:11,007
Look. If you dip it in the sauce
like this…

464
00:34:26,439 --> 00:34:27,356
Want some, huh?

465
00:34:27,440 --> 00:34:29,067
No way. I don't want any.

466
00:34:32,987 --> 00:34:34,113
Then

467
00:34:34,822 --> 00:34:36,240
just try the end.

468
00:34:36,324 --> 00:34:38,201
-I'll cut it off for you.
-In that case…

469
00:34:39,077 --> 00:34:40,369
No foot shape.

470
00:34:41,496 --> 00:34:42,622
Seriously.

471
00:34:48,211 --> 00:34:49,295
Here.

472
00:35:03,976 --> 00:35:04,811
Isn't it good?

473
00:35:05,478 --> 00:35:06,354
It's good, right?

474
00:35:07,230 --> 00:35:09,899
I guess it's not bad.

475
00:35:35,007 --> 00:35:38,511
Do you know how they make
these boneless chicken feet?

476
00:35:39,011 --> 00:35:39,846
No, I don't.

477
00:35:39,929 --> 00:35:45,726
The owner gnaws the bones out
one by one, like this.

478
00:35:46,811 --> 00:35:49,605
That's how he makes them boneless.

479
00:35:49,689 --> 00:35:52,191
How's everything? Good?

480
00:35:54,360 --> 00:35:55,403
Enjoy.

481
00:36:01,242 --> 00:36:02,285
He's got strong teeth.

482
00:36:09,750 --> 00:36:11,169
I was just kidding.

483
00:36:24,432 --> 00:36:26,559
All right, then. Go on in.

484
00:36:27,643 --> 00:36:30,730
Bet you'll sleep well tonight
after that big meal.

485
00:36:31,731 --> 00:36:32,565
Good night.

486
00:36:34,400 --> 00:36:36,319
Don't forget about the hospital tomorrow.

487
00:36:46,537 --> 00:36:48,789
The Hangang River date.

488
00:36:48,873 --> 00:36:52,877
Better do it before I forget. Quick.

489
00:36:55,213 --> 00:36:58,132
Hye-ju and I-hyeok walk

490
00:36:58,216 --> 00:37:01,677
side by side along the Hangang River.

491
00:37:03,596 --> 00:37:05,097
THEIR HANDS ALMOST BRUSH

492
00:37:05,181 --> 00:37:08,517
THE TWO ARE ACUTELY AWARE OF EACH OTHER

493
00:37:43,094 --> 00:37:44,053
Ma'am.

494
00:37:44,136 --> 00:37:45,179
(HOLDING HER IN HIS ARMS)

495
00:37:45,263 --> 00:37:46,305
Are you all right?

496
00:37:48,057 --> 00:37:49,267
Yeah.

497
00:37:49,350 --> 00:37:51,227
Are you sure you don't need
to go to the hospital?

498
00:37:51,852 --> 00:37:52,687
I'm okay.

499
00:37:52,770 --> 00:37:54,272
(TREMBLING)

500
00:37:55,022 --> 00:37:56,023
(STARTLED)

501
00:37:56,107 --> 00:37:57,400
You're bleeding!

502
00:37:59,527 --> 00:38:02,947
I-HYEOK HIDES HIS WOUND AS IF IT'S NOTHING

503
00:38:03,030 --> 00:38:06,075
As long as you're not hurt, I'm fine.

504
00:38:08,411 --> 00:38:14,292
I-HYEOK GAZES AT HYE-JU WISTFULLY

505
00:38:16,585 --> 00:38:18,087
That's it. That's more like it.

506
00:38:18,170 --> 00:38:19,630
He likes her,

507
00:38:19,714 --> 00:38:22,508
so he doesn't care if he gets hurt
as long as she's okay.

508
00:38:23,134 --> 00:38:24,468
I'm fine.

509
00:38:24,552 --> 00:38:25,428
I'm not.

510
00:38:25,511 --> 00:38:26,887
I don't think I got hit.

511
00:38:26,971 --> 00:38:28,556
That can't be good for my heart.

512
00:38:31,517 --> 00:38:33,769
Real life is nothing like the dramas.

513
00:38:59,962 --> 00:39:02,256
How about changing your sleep pattern?

514
00:39:03,174 --> 00:39:05,343
I was in the zone last night.

515
00:39:05,426 --> 00:39:07,762
It was like I was possessed.

516
00:39:08,346 --> 00:39:11,265
They say great writers
write a set amount every day,

517
00:39:11,349 --> 00:39:13,559
no matter how they feel.

518
00:39:13,642 --> 00:39:17,605
Yeah, well,
I'm still just a lousy rookie writer.

519
00:39:20,566 --> 00:39:21,400
What's the matter?

520
00:39:40,169 --> 00:39:41,045
It's nothing.

521
00:39:59,438 --> 00:40:00,773
I'll handle it.

522
00:40:05,945 --> 00:40:07,029
Ma'am.

523
00:40:07,113 --> 00:40:08,197
-Yes?
-Excuse me.

524
00:40:08,280 --> 00:40:09,824
May I see your phone?

525
00:40:09,907 --> 00:40:11,117
Why?

526
00:40:11,200 --> 00:40:12,618
I heard a camera click.

527
00:40:12,701 --> 00:40:14,829
Just making sure
you didn't take a photo of us.

528
00:40:14,912 --> 00:40:15,996
What?

529
00:40:16,080 --> 00:40:17,915
Why would I take a photo of you people?

530
00:40:17,998 --> 00:40:19,708
I'm just being careful.

531
00:40:19,792 --> 00:40:22,211
-Please excuse me.
-No!

532
00:40:22,837 --> 00:40:24,672
What's Mr. Yoon doing?

533
00:40:24,755 --> 00:40:27,299
He's checking
whether she took a picture of me.

534
00:40:27,383 --> 00:40:29,718
What? Why would she take a picture of you?

535
00:40:29,802 --> 00:40:33,305
She could be a paparazzo
or a reporter in disguise.

536
00:40:33,389 --> 00:40:34,432
What?

537
00:40:34,515 --> 00:40:38,519
Listen, we're not even allowed
to use our phones while we're working!

538
00:40:38,602 --> 00:40:40,646
Isn't this a bit much?

539
00:40:40,729 --> 00:40:42,523
Keep your opinions to yourself.

540
00:40:44,275 --> 00:40:47,069
People are watching.
Talk to her somewhere quiet.

541
00:40:56,328 --> 00:40:57,329
No!

542
00:41:38,787 --> 00:41:39,622
Sir?

543
00:41:40,998 --> 00:41:42,875
Sir!

544
00:41:42,958 --> 00:41:47,630
Seriously,
I swear I didn't take any photos.

545
00:41:48,214 --> 00:41:49,215
Look.

546
00:41:51,383 --> 00:41:54,303
We're not allowed to use our phones
while we're cleaning,

547
00:41:54,386 --> 00:41:57,014
but I was texting my daughter.

548
00:41:57,598 --> 00:41:59,099
That's why I couldn't show him.

549
00:42:00,017 --> 00:42:02,019
Do you think he'll report me?

550
00:42:02,603 --> 00:42:04,730
They've gone to report me, right?

551
00:42:06,190 --> 00:42:08,651
Just explain what happened.
I'll talk to them too.

552
00:42:08,734 --> 00:42:10,819
Thank you, I appreciate it.

553
00:42:10,903 --> 00:42:13,322
I didn't take any photos.
He just came up to me.

554
00:42:30,256 --> 00:42:33,717
You took off like something happened,
yet here you are,

555
00:42:34,218 --> 00:42:35,052
just chilling.

556
00:42:35,970 --> 00:42:37,096
Go check on the cleaner.

557
00:42:38,764 --> 00:42:39,765
Yes, sir.

558
00:42:39,848 --> 00:42:42,309
I checked her phone.
There were no photos of you.

559
00:42:42,393 --> 00:42:43,727
Mr. Yoon, go check it.

560
00:42:44,645 --> 00:42:46,647
Yes, sir. Understood.

561
00:42:51,360 --> 00:42:54,655
Do you always go around accusing people
and saying whatever you want?

562
00:42:54,738 --> 00:42:57,575
That's OCD, paranoia,
or something like that.

563
00:42:57,658 --> 00:42:59,243
It's your problem.

564
00:42:59,326 --> 00:43:00,494
Well,

565
00:43:00,578 --> 00:43:02,663
now that you're here, have a seat.

566
00:43:07,543 --> 00:43:10,629
I heard you and Ho-rang
tested the charging rate.

567
00:43:11,630 --> 00:43:16,760
Since it's not exactly normal for a person
to charge an artificial heart,

568
00:43:16,844 --> 00:43:22,224
I'd like to run a few tests
to make sure nothing's wrong with you.

569
00:43:22,308 --> 00:43:23,142
Right.

570
00:43:23,225 --> 00:43:25,477
We're here for different tests.

571
00:43:25,561 --> 00:43:27,354
Did you have to call us in together?

572
00:43:27,438 --> 00:43:30,524
I don't want to be around
some power-tripping narcissist either.

573
00:43:31,650 --> 00:43:33,027
Can I go get my tests now?

574
00:43:33,110 --> 00:43:34,320
-Well…
-Ms. Na.

575
00:43:34,403 --> 00:43:36,697
You don't know my story,
so watch what you say.

576
00:43:36,780 --> 00:43:39,783
Don't act like your bad manners
come with some backstory.

577
00:43:39,867 --> 00:43:44,413
You think you're some paragon of virtue?

578
00:43:44,496 --> 00:43:47,916
It's always the ones
with character flaws who ask that.

579
00:43:48,000 --> 00:43:50,044
-Ms. Na Bo-bae!
-What, Mr. Baek Ho-rang?

580
00:43:51,295 --> 00:43:52,504
Excuse me, you two.

581
00:43:52,588 --> 00:43:54,423
-Let's do the tests!
-Where do I go?

582
00:44:03,974 --> 00:44:06,894
Did you have heart surgery?
That's a big scar.

583
00:44:07,853 --> 00:44:11,440
I was struck by lightning
when I was a kid.

584
00:44:11,523 --> 00:44:12,441
It's from that.

585
00:44:12,524 --> 00:44:15,235
-Lightning?
-Yeah. Pretty unusual, right?

586
00:44:15,819 --> 00:44:16,945
Yes, it is.

587
00:44:19,907 --> 00:44:22,076
I checked,
but there were no photos of you.

588
00:44:22,576 --> 00:44:24,119
No deleted photos either.

589
00:44:28,957 --> 00:44:32,169
Make sure to apologize to her
and compensate her properly.

590
00:44:33,087 --> 00:44:34,088
Yes, sir.

591
00:44:45,599 --> 00:44:46,725
Shall I call her back?

592
00:44:47,434 --> 00:44:48,394
Don't bother.

593
00:44:49,269 --> 00:44:50,270
We'll go separately.

594
00:45:39,486 --> 00:45:40,654
Mother, are you asleep?

595
00:45:48,746 --> 00:45:49,663
Stepmom.

596
00:45:53,625 --> 00:45:54,793
Hey, lady.

597
00:45:59,882 --> 00:46:01,258
I can't visit for a while.

598
00:46:04,094 --> 00:46:06,889
I've found something more interesting
than watching you.

599
00:46:10,225 --> 00:46:11,101
Who is this woman?

600
00:46:11,185 --> 00:46:13,645
They looked pretty close.
Maybe she's his girlfriend?

601
00:46:16,648 --> 00:46:18,233
Baek Ho-rang's girlfriend?

602
00:46:20,444 --> 00:46:22,237
Got any other photos of her?

603
00:46:22,321 --> 00:46:23,363
No, not yet.

604
00:46:26,158 --> 00:46:28,035
Follow him around the clock.

605
00:46:28,118 --> 00:46:29,453
-Okay?
-Yes, sir.

606
00:46:30,120 --> 00:46:31,580
And find out more about her.

607
00:46:31,663 --> 00:46:32,498
Yes, sir.

608
00:46:33,999 --> 00:46:34,875
Cheers.

609
00:46:42,174 --> 00:46:44,718
Going all out already?
You just had your appendix out.

610
00:46:44,802 --> 00:46:46,011
I'm fine now.

611
00:46:46,094 --> 00:46:48,305
Excuse me, could we get some chopsticks?

612
00:46:48,388 --> 00:46:50,474
Gonna drink till I drop. Don't stop me.

613
00:46:51,350 --> 00:46:53,936
What if Ji-hye gets mad at me
for letting you drink?

614
00:46:54,019 --> 00:46:55,938
Your sister really scares me.

615
00:46:56,021 --> 00:46:57,231
It's okay. I moved out.

616
00:46:57,314 --> 00:46:58,899
Huh? When?

617
00:47:00,067 --> 00:47:00,901
Yesterday.

618
00:47:00,984 --> 00:47:01,819
No way. Damn.

619
00:47:01,902 --> 00:47:04,613
Why didn't you tell me?

620
00:47:05,531 --> 00:47:06,365
-Well…
-Yeah?

621
00:47:07,324 --> 00:47:08,617
Actually…

622
00:47:09,576 --> 00:47:10,786
You're out of your mind.

623
00:47:11,370 --> 00:47:13,664
What if your sister and brother
find out you lied?

624
00:47:13,747 --> 00:47:16,667
Your sister's gonna kill you
if you keep this up.

625
00:47:16,750 --> 00:47:18,502
No. Listen.

626
00:47:19,002 --> 00:47:20,879
Say I spend three months with Mr. Baek,

627
00:47:20,963 --> 00:47:23,465
fulfill our contract,
and finish my bucket list.

628
00:47:24,049 --> 00:47:25,509
Then I work it into my script.

629
00:47:25,592 --> 00:47:28,053
-Work it in.
-Then I renew my writing contract.

630
00:47:28,136 --> 00:47:29,137
-Renew it.
-Then…

631
00:47:30,931 --> 00:47:33,684
-It won't be a lie anymore.
-What if they don't renew it?

632
00:47:35,269 --> 00:47:39,064
Your brother's moving to Daejeon.
Your sister's moving in with her husband.

633
00:47:39,147 --> 00:47:41,775
And that chaebol will kick you out
once the contract's up.

634
00:47:41,859 --> 00:47:43,735
Then what? You'll have nowhere to go.

635
00:47:43,819 --> 00:47:45,654
If they don't renew my contract,

636
00:47:46,154 --> 00:47:48,115
I'll have to move back in with my parents.

637
00:47:48,699 --> 00:47:49,575
No plan, huh?

638
00:47:51,910 --> 00:47:53,412
You're driving me up the wall.

639
00:47:53,996 --> 00:47:54,955
I have it worse.

640
00:47:55,038 --> 00:47:59,543
That chaebol whose name means "tiger."
What if he finds out about your powers?

641
00:47:59,626 --> 00:48:02,212
You said he has no idea
why you can charge his heart.

642
00:48:02,296 --> 00:48:06,341
He doesn't get zapped when I touch him.
I don't think he'll ever find out.

643
00:48:06,425 --> 00:48:07,676
He just doesn't know yet.

644
00:48:07,759 --> 00:48:09,720
What are you gonna do

645
00:48:09,803 --> 00:48:13,307
if you get angry or too excited
and blow out the lights?

646
00:48:14,349 --> 00:48:16,018
-You think so?
-"You think so"?

647
00:48:18,270 --> 00:48:21,899
Hey, don't you know rich snobs sue
at the drop of a hat?

648
00:48:21,982 --> 00:48:26,028
What if he sues you
for lying about your powers?

649
00:48:27,195 --> 00:48:28,322
You're right.

650
00:48:28,405 --> 00:48:30,532
I have to make sure he never finds out.

651
00:48:54,222 --> 00:48:55,515
What time is it?

652
00:48:55,599 --> 00:48:57,851
Huh? We have to go.

653
00:48:58,936 --> 00:49:03,065
Hey, Bo-bae. Wake up.

654
00:49:03,732 --> 00:49:05,776
Hey, wake up. We have to go.

655
00:49:06,276 --> 00:49:08,820
Wake up.

656
00:49:10,030 --> 00:49:12,157
Sorry. We're leaving. Just a second.

657
00:49:12,240 --> 00:49:13,617
DIRECTOR YEOM MIN-KYU

658
00:49:16,328 --> 00:49:19,623
Well, if it isn't my favorite director!

659
00:49:20,123 --> 00:49:21,291
Right now?

660
00:49:22,167 --> 00:49:23,085
Yes.

661
00:49:24,252 --> 00:49:26,421
I had a few drinks,
but I'm not that drunk.

662
00:49:27,422 --> 00:49:28,548
No.

663
00:49:28,632 --> 00:49:31,009
Yes, I'll be right there.

664
00:49:32,552 --> 00:49:35,180
What am I going to do with her? Seriously.

665
00:49:35,764 --> 00:49:38,976
Hey, wake up.
We really have to go. Damn it.

666
00:49:40,227 --> 00:49:42,396
Crap. What am I supposed to do with her?

667
00:49:43,188 --> 00:49:44,356
Someone's calling her.

668
00:49:52,239 --> 00:49:54,866
You little punk! Perfect timing.

669
00:49:56,243 --> 00:49:57,244
Hey.

670
00:49:58,537 --> 00:50:00,664
Damn it. Seriously.

671
00:50:05,752 --> 00:50:07,004
-Eun-ho! Hey.
-Ms. Cho.

672
00:50:07,087 --> 00:50:09,047
Eun-ho, thank you so much.

673
00:50:09,548 --> 00:50:11,133
I should take her home,

674
00:50:11,216 --> 00:50:13,593
but Director Yeom suddenly put me to work.

675
00:50:13,677 --> 00:50:14,636
-Right.
-Yeah.

676
00:50:14,720 --> 00:50:16,388
I know you two are close, so…

677
00:50:16,471 --> 00:50:18,056
Yes, I'll take care of Bo-bae.

678
00:50:18,140 --> 00:50:19,766
Okay. Thank you so much.

679
00:50:19,850 --> 00:50:20,684
No problem.

680
00:50:21,852 --> 00:50:23,729
Oh, that's right.

681
00:50:23,812 --> 00:50:26,106
You know Bo-bae doesn't like
being touched, right?

682
00:50:26,189 --> 00:50:27,858
-Yes.
-Don't try to support her.

683
00:50:27,941 --> 00:50:30,402
Touch her through her clothes
if you need to.

684
00:50:30,485 --> 00:50:33,238
Just wake her up and get her home, please.

685
00:50:33,321 --> 00:50:35,323
-Yes, got it.
-Please look after her.

686
00:50:35,407 --> 00:50:36,533
Bye.

687
00:50:36,616 --> 00:50:38,493
Wake up already, Na Bo-bae!

688
00:50:38,577 --> 00:50:39,870
Go, damn it.

689
00:50:39,953 --> 00:50:41,788
Jeez, I'm off, then.

690
00:50:41,872 --> 00:50:42,956
All right.

691
00:50:44,875 --> 00:50:45,709
Bo-bae.

692
00:50:45,792 --> 00:50:47,252
Damn it.

693
00:50:48,962 --> 00:50:50,130
I mean…

694
00:50:50,756 --> 00:50:55,260
Just because he makes a lot of money
and has a fancy business card,

695
00:50:55,343 --> 00:50:58,555
does he think he can treat a cleaner
however he wants?

696
00:51:00,932 --> 00:51:02,517
Wow, she's really drunk.

697
00:51:04,644 --> 00:51:06,104
Why, you…

698
00:51:06,188 --> 00:51:07,022
Damn it.

699
00:51:11,193 --> 00:51:12,569
Bo-bae, let's go.

700
00:51:12,652 --> 00:51:14,905
You little…

701
00:51:15,614 --> 00:51:16,948
Let's go. Get up.

702
00:51:25,749 --> 00:51:27,084
Bo-bae, come here.

703
00:51:39,554 --> 00:51:40,388
Wow!

704
00:51:42,474 --> 00:51:43,391
Bo-bae!

705
00:51:50,690 --> 00:51:53,735
What if the battery dies?
Why isn't she back yet? Damn it.

706
00:52:07,999 --> 00:52:09,835
I used to eat this a lot as a kid.

707
00:52:09,918 --> 00:52:12,504
You know what? He was my favorite.

708
00:52:13,296 --> 00:52:16,758
He can generate electricity too,
and he's super strong.

709
00:52:17,259 --> 00:52:18,093
Me too.

710
00:52:18,677 --> 00:52:20,804
Bet that's why Pikachu
is everyone's favorite.

711
00:52:27,811 --> 00:52:30,147
So you should stop hiding it from me and…

712
00:52:30,230 --> 00:52:31,064
What's this?

713
00:52:34,067 --> 00:52:35,485
RUBBER GLOVE

714
00:52:37,654 --> 00:52:38,613
"Rubber glove"?

715
00:52:40,282 --> 00:52:41,783
Forget it. I'm not answering.

716
00:52:42,284 --> 00:52:45,078
This douchebag.
I can't stand the sight of him.

717
00:52:46,037 --> 00:52:49,583
Go on. So you like Pikachu too?

718
00:52:52,502 --> 00:52:53,336
Yes.

719
00:52:54,963 --> 00:52:56,047
Very much.

720
00:52:56,548 --> 00:52:59,885
I didn't know Pikachu was this popular.

721
00:53:00,677 --> 00:53:03,388
The person you're calling is unavailable.

722
00:53:03,471 --> 00:53:05,390
Please call back later.

723
00:53:05,473 --> 00:53:06,641
She's not picking up?

724
00:53:07,684 --> 00:53:08,518
PORTABLE CHARGER

725
00:53:08,602 --> 00:53:10,187
Come home right now.

726
00:53:10,937 --> 00:53:15,567
Get within a ten-meter radius of me!

727
00:53:20,614 --> 00:53:21,448
Read it.

728
00:53:24,367 --> 00:53:25,368
Don't tell me…

729
00:53:25,452 --> 00:53:27,871
Is she not gonna come back at all?

730
00:53:29,831 --> 00:53:33,084
Twenty-five hours
since separating from Na Bo-bae.

731
00:53:38,256 --> 00:53:39,299
Dead.

732
00:53:40,008 --> 00:53:41,009
DEAD

733
00:53:50,435 --> 00:53:53,188
It's all just pointless worries.

734
00:53:54,022 --> 00:53:58,068
I need to clear my mind
of distracting thoughts and worries.

735
00:54:09,704 --> 00:54:14,501
As you breathe in,
feel positive energy fill you.

736
00:54:15,752 --> 00:54:21,800
As you breathe out,
release all the negative energy.

737
00:54:23,301 --> 00:54:28,223
When you exhale,
let go of the person troubling you.

738
00:54:29,474 --> 00:54:33,520
Mr. Baek Ho-rang.
A power-tripping narcissist.

739
00:54:33,603 --> 00:54:35,230
You'd be dead without me.

740
00:54:35,313 --> 00:54:38,358
Scared? Anxious? Losing your mind?

741
00:54:38,858 --> 00:54:39,859
No!

742
00:54:42,821 --> 00:54:43,989
What the…

743
00:54:45,699 --> 00:54:46,825
Damn it.

744
00:54:59,879 --> 00:55:01,923
Bo-bae, you live here now?

745
00:55:02,007 --> 00:55:02,882
Yeah.

746
00:55:02,966 --> 00:55:04,342
Darn it.

747
00:55:05,093 --> 00:55:08,513
This thing's just like its owner. Damn it.

748
00:55:15,020 --> 00:55:15,979
Seriously…

749
00:55:19,232 --> 00:55:21,609
Bo-bae, I don't think
this is the right place.

750
00:55:22,235 --> 00:55:24,404
It's way too big.
Look again. Are you sure?

751
00:55:24,487 --> 00:55:26,448
It's the right place. Baek Ho--

752
00:55:26,531 --> 00:55:27,532
Our arrangement

753
00:55:28,033 --> 00:55:31,036
stays strictly between us.

754
00:55:34,748 --> 00:55:35,665
Actually, no.

755
00:55:35,749 --> 00:55:37,667
It's not here.

756
00:55:38,752 --> 00:55:40,337
Where is it? I'll take you home.

757
00:55:40,420 --> 00:55:42,422
No!

758
00:55:43,882 --> 00:55:46,217
It's the house next door. Right next door.

759
00:55:47,385 --> 00:55:49,012
I'm so drunk, aren't I?

760
00:55:53,850 --> 00:55:55,894
Here. This is it.

761
00:55:55,977 --> 00:55:57,729
I'll head in. Go on home, Eun-ho.

762
00:55:58,313 --> 00:55:59,898
-I'll go after you go--
-No!

763
00:56:01,191 --> 00:56:02,692
I'm home already. No need.

764
00:56:05,528 --> 00:56:09,157
Save those lovey-dovey eyes
for your melodramas.

765
00:56:09,240 --> 00:56:11,451
When did I ever give you lovey-dovey eyes?

766
00:56:32,305 --> 00:56:34,933
I was just looking.
You're the one who got butterflies.

767
00:56:47,946 --> 00:56:49,322
As if!

768
00:56:49,989 --> 00:56:52,534
I said go home. Go already!

769
00:56:52,617 --> 00:56:53,952
Okay, Bo-bae. Calm down.

770
00:56:54,035 --> 00:56:55,453
You need to calm down.

771
00:56:55,537 --> 00:56:57,288
-I'm off.
-Yeah, bye.

772
00:56:57,372 --> 00:56:58,581
-Calm down, Bo-bae.
-Yeah.

773
00:56:58,665 --> 00:57:01,584
I'm calming down right now, Eun-ho. Bye.

774
00:57:16,224 --> 00:57:17,684
I think he sometimes

775
00:57:18,184 --> 00:57:20,895
forgets I've been single my whole life.

776
00:57:25,442 --> 00:57:27,152
Damn.

777
00:57:28,653 --> 00:57:32,782
Crap, my heart's still pounding.

778
00:57:36,244 --> 00:57:37,829
That hurts.

779
00:57:37,912 --> 00:57:39,038
Oh God.

780
00:57:40,665 --> 00:57:42,876
Oh no! I'm bleeding!

781
00:57:45,003 --> 00:57:46,796
It hurts.

782
00:57:47,755 --> 00:57:49,424
Huh?

783
00:57:53,678 --> 00:57:54,512
What?

784
00:58:13,531 --> 00:58:14,866
Ms. Na Bo-bae?

785
00:58:16,701 --> 00:58:19,579
Oh no. What if I just caused a blackout?

786
00:58:22,165 --> 00:58:23,416
Damn it.

787
00:58:30,632 --> 00:58:31,549
Click.

788
00:58:34,427 --> 00:58:35,470
Pika.

789
00:58:37,305 --> 00:58:38,431
Pika.

790
00:58:39,682 --> 00:58:45,063
Pikachu!

791
00:58:51,611 --> 00:58:52,737
Why didn't it work?

792
00:58:54,447 --> 00:58:55,782
What's going on?

793
00:58:57,825 --> 00:59:00,328
Mr. Baek Ho-rang!

794
00:59:01,412 --> 00:59:02,330
Huh?

795
00:59:02,997 --> 00:59:05,500
Mr. Baek, did you fall?

796
00:59:06,668 --> 00:59:09,045
Oh no. What do I do?

797
00:59:11,089 --> 00:59:14,300
Mr. Baek Ho-rang, I'm coming!

798
00:59:14,384 --> 00:59:15,677
Hold on.

799
00:59:16,719 --> 00:59:18,888
Mr. Baek!

800
00:59:18,972 --> 00:59:19,806
I'll…

801
00:59:19,889 --> 00:59:22,976
Huh? Where is he?

802
00:59:24,060 --> 00:59:24,894
Huh?

803
00:59:25,395 --> 00:59:27,272
Here, right? Here!

804
00:59:27,355 --> 00:59:28,940
Don't open it!

805
00:59:29,816 --> 00:59:31,401
I told you not to come in!

806
00:59:31,484 --> 00:59:34,028
-Are you hurt? Are you okay?
-Ms. Na!

807
00:59:34,112 --> 00:59:35,780
I'm not wearing anything right now!

808
00:59:35,863 --> 00:59:38,825
I can't see anything anyway.

809
00:59:41,202 --> 00:59:42,287
You're hurt.

810
00:59:42,370 --> 00:59:44,789
Hold my hand. Can you see it?

811
00:59:44,872 --> 00:59:47,333
Well, if I could,
that'd be an even bigger problem!

812
00:59:48,251 --> 00:59:52,463
Hey, there's a bathrobe over there.
Just hand it to me.

813
00:59:52,547 --> 00:59:54,966
-Bathrobe?
-Yes, a bathrobe.

814
00:59:55,049 --> 00:59:56,217
It's here.

815
00:59:56,301 --> 00:59:57,176
Here.

816
00:59:57,260 --> 00:59:59,512
-Here. Grab it.
-Okay.

817
00:59:59,596 --> 01:00:00,763
-Where is it?
-Right here.

818
01:00:23,494 --> 01:00:24,704
You reek of alcohol.

819
01:00:25,288 --> 01:00:26,873
I'm sorry.

820
01:02:21,988 --> 01:02:26,576
Subtitle translation by: Sung In Jang
